@startuml "Command - Account (Problem) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title The teller's undo, three honest attempts

package "stage one" {
  class OneStepAccount {
    - balance : Money
    - lastKind : String
    - lastAmount : Money
    + deposit(Money)
    + withdraw(Money)
    + undo()
  }
  note bottom of OneStepAccount
    <b>One step only.</b> A second undo finds nothing.
    Two of its fields are bookkeeping for a screen.
  end note
}

package "stage two" {
  class HistoryAccount {
    - balance : Money
    - done : Deque<Entry>
    - undone : Deque<Entry>
    + deposit(Money)
    + withdraw(Money)
    + undo()
    + redo()
    + journal() : List<String>
    + canUndo() : boolean
    + canRedo() : boolean
  }
  note bottom of HistoryAccount
    <b>Undo, redo and a journal, all on the account.</b>
    Eight public operations, three of them banking.
    Each operation lives in three places.
  end note
}

package "stage three" {
  class Teller {
    - done : Deque<Entry>
    + deposit(Account, Money)
    + withdraw(Account, Money)
    + transfer(Account, Account, Money)
    + undo()
    + redo()
  }
  class Account {
    + deposit(Money)
    + withdraw(Money)
  }
  enum Kind {
    DEPOSIT
    WITHDRAW
  }
  Teller ..> Account
  Teller ..> Kind
  note bottom of Teller
    <b>The account is clean again.</b> The teller
    branches on a kind to undo and to redo.
    transfer() reuses withdraw() and deposit(),
    records two entries, and one undo takes
    back only the deposit.
  end note
}

OneStepAccount -[hidden]right- HistoryAccount
HistoryAccount -[hidden]right- Teller
@enduml
